   "gap_category": "other:multi_source_obligation",
   "why_not_expressible": "An obligation has exactly one effect source (obligations.py:127 'source: Identifier'). effect_joins (mechanism 8) can attach a second source, but only effects committed before/not after the primary effect (obligations.py:81 timing Literal['before','not_after']; _join_context limit at obligations.py:290), so an any-channel obligation written as 'primary OR join' is a known 0 whenever the other-channel effect comes later. Not one of the five categories: the target is computable; the missing piece is an any-of over two effect inventories.",
   "mechanism_sketch": "effects.required_when@1 'sources': [{source, effect_match}, ...] witnessed by any listed inventory, known 0 only when every listed inventory is closed; or, smaller, effect_joins timing 'any' (whole episode, complete inventory) so 'primary OR join' is order-independent.",
   "note": "The task's listed tools are Gmail, Sheets and Slack (no calendar); Luna found google_calendar_create_detailed_event via search. An invite may be a calendar event with attendees or an email to employee + manager; a calendar-only check would known-0 the email path.",
   "reused_by": [
    "hr.buddy_assignment (buddy notice by Gmail or Slack)"
   ]
  },
